{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Whose daughter are you? Tell, etc.</b> He joined the two questions together, to indicate that he had no doubt whether she was of Abraham's family — for if he were in doubt, it would not befit him to ask whether there was lodging until he knew whether the path was proper before him. Rather, he surely trusted in HaShem that his way had succeeded, and what he asked in ״Whose daughter are you?״ was merely what her father's name was, etc. And before she would answer, he said ״Is there room in your father's house,״ etc., for this matter would not change depending on her answer to whose daughter she was, etc. Understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:06.929676313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}